comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-18T08:41:08.209Z","harness:codex","Focused implementation child of existing public-surface consistency programme for GH-1494, not a second defect owner. Complete strict all-status intake plus parent full metadata/history and existing closed children show no matching delivery task. The programme remains open for website/plugin/count/terminology acceptance; this child closes only canonical examples with executable diagnostic proof."
  "2026-10-18T08:54:39.969Z","harness:codex","Verification: canonical list/plan diagnostics plus every core help narrative pass the deprecated-alias registry guard. List examples were shortened while preserving their intent so the canonical spelling fits the existing 2000-token recovery budget instead of losing its examples to degradation. Typecheck, SDK compatibility (zero classified public changes), complete command grammar, and flag-invocation parity passed. Full coverage is still running; it caught the new encoding alias on internal worker discovery, which will be corrected before final verification."
  "2026-10-18T09:51:27.667Z","harness:codex","Completed implementation proof: all core help narratives are checked against the deprecated-alias registry; real list projection and plan recovery examples are canonical and remain within the existing diagnostic ceiling. Shared candidate full-source run passed 10662 tests and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. Both linked item verification commands passed, and all 12 changed source/docs/test artifacts matched the isolated coverage checkout byte for byte. Changelog generation remains owned by latest pm-changelog; broader public-surface programme pm-wg07 remains open for its other acceptance criteria."
  "2026-10-18T09:57:46.177Z","harness:codex","Final local static, graph, record-integrity, bounded mutation, serial startup/transport, full-source exact coverage, and packed consumer gates passed. Canonical error examples retain the existing output budget, and all core help examples are guarded by the SDK alias registry. Implementation is complete for this focused child; the broad parent retains its unrelated consistency acceptance criteria."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-18T09:16:46.141Z","harness:codex","Canonical command spellings can push a diagnostic over its existing token ceiling. Preserve concise, executable examples and test the real bounded refusal, rather than only searching source strings or raising the budget."
